# Playwright's per-run report and screenshots, written on a failing spec.
test-results/

# `tools/bench.mjs`'s results, and the reason they are not a baseline: **a frame
# rate is a fact about a card, a window and a preset, and none of those three are
# a property of the build.** The suite's own numbers are committed because
# SwiftShader at 480x300 is the same rasteriser on every machine that runs it -
# `tools/e2e/baseline.json` is comparable because it is pinned to one. A bench run
# on an RX 6800 at 2560x1440 is not comparable to anything, and committing one
# would invite the reading that it is a floor or a ceiling. It is neither: it is
# one machine's answer on one afternoon.
bench/

# Half-finished extractions from the module split. `check.sh` globs `src/*.js` and
# `wired.mjs` is handed the same list, so a file with any other extension sits in
# the module folder and is read by no gate at all - which is how a one-line
# `src/graphics.js.deferred` spent three commits in the tree.
*.deferred
*.bak
*.orig

# The prop library and its maps are build artefacts: `meshes/*.glb` and
# `meshes/tex/*.png` are 77 MB written by the pages in `meshes/build-*.html` and by
# the dev server's `/__save` hook - **and the two wardrobe folders are the same
# thing**, `meshes/faces/*.glb` and `meshes/hats/*.glb`, written by
# `build-face.html` and `build-hat.html` through the same hook with a `dir`.
# **Everything in `meshes/` that is not one of those is source** - the three
# modules every builder page imports, and the builder pages themselves, which are
# the only way to regenerate the artefacts - so the ignore is a deny with
# exceptions rather than a deny of the folder. A clone with these in it can build
# the county; a clone without them cannot build the game, cannot run
# `tools/check.sh`, and cannot run `tools/wired.mjs` at all, since it is handed
# all three modules by name.
#/meshes/*
!/meshes/palette.js
!/meshes/maps.js
!/meshes/biomes.js
!/meshes/build-*.html

# `.kilo/` holds the session's plans and skills, and `references/` whatever was
# read in to write them. Neither is the game.
.kilo/
references/